<title>HONG KONG: Goldlion interim net rises 14.01 pct.</title>
<headline>Goldlion interim net rises 14.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   18.1   vs  17.3</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0    vs  6.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs  3.06 gain (see note)</p>
<p>    Net			    145.96 vs  128.02</p>
<p>    Turnover		     640.16 vs  576.27</p>
<p>    Company name		 Goldlion Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 14-17, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 22, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Goldlion Holdings is a men's clothing manufacturer.</p>
<p>Comparative exceptional items has been reclassified and included in the operating profit balance. The remaining balance of HK$3.06 million represents the net surplus arising from repurchase and subsequent cancellation of convertible bonds during the 1995 year.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
